---
title: "Image and layout building blocks"
description: "Public primitive props, callbacks, methods and styling."
---

# Image and layout building blocks

All optional props without a default remain `undefined`. `class` accepts Svelte `ClassValue`; `style` is a CSS string.

These primitives require and provide no cropper context. Supply their data and callbacks explicitly. Unless listed, they have no exported instance methods. Container children are optional `Snippet` values rendered without arguments.

<h2 id="cropper-wrapper">CropperWrapper</h2>

Fades its children in when the cropper has state and is loaded. It keeps children mounted while loading. Its optional cropper needs getState, isLoading and isLoaded.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `cropper` | `CropperWrapperSource` | `undefined` |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `children` | `Snippet` | `undefined` |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `undefined` |

`CropperWrapperSource` is a local name for this exact structural contract, not an exported type:

```ts
interface CropperWrapperSource {
	getState: () => CropperState | null;
	isLoading: () => boolean;
	isLoaded: () => boolean;
}
```

A matching cropper or preview snippet argument can be spread directly into this primitive.

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="stretchable-boundary">StretchableBoundary</h2>

Registers boundary measurement with the owning cropper or preview. Exposes `reset(): void` and `stretchTo(size: Size | null): Promise<Size | null>` through bind:this, typed as StretchableBoundaryMethods. Registration cleanup runs on destruction.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `registerBoundary` | `RegisterBoundary` | `undefined` |
| `stretchAlgorithm` | `BoundaryStretchAlgorithm` | `stretchCropperBoundary` |
| `sizeAlgorithm` | `BoundarySizeAlgorithm` | `fillLayoutBoundary` |
| `children` | `Snippet` | `undefined` |

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="cropper-background-wrapper">CropperBackgroundWrapper</h2>

Connects TransformableImage to transformImage and transformImageEnd. The cropper also supplies getTransitions. Active transitions disable gestures. An omitted timeout uses the gesture primitive default of 500 ms.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `cropper` | `CropperBackgroundWrapperSource` | Required |
| `rotateImage` | `boolean` \| `RotateImageOptions` | `false` |
| `scaleImage` | `boolean` \| `ScaleImageOptions` | `true` |
| `moveImage` | `boolean` \| `MoveImageOptions` | `true` |
| `children` | `Snippet` | `undefined` |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `timeout` | `number` | `undefined` |
| `onEvent` | `TransformableImageProps['onEvent']` | `undefined` |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `undefined` |

`CropperBackgroundWrapperSource` is a local name for this exact structural contract, not an exported type:

```ts
interface CropperBackgroundWrapperSource {
	transformImage: (transform: ImageTransform) => void;
	transformImageEnd: () => void;
	getTransitions: () => CropperTransitions;
}
```

A matching cropper or preview snippet argument can be spread directly into this primitive.

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="cropper-background-image">CropperBackgroundImage</h2>

Draws the displayed image using getBackgroundStyle. The cropper supplies getState, getTransitions and getImage. Forward attachSource from a background snippet for canvas export.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `cropper` | `CropperBackgroundImageSource` | Required |
| `crossOrigin` | `'anonymous'` \| `'use-credentials'` \| `boolean` | `true` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `attachSource` | `AttachBackgroundSource` | `undefined` |

`CropperBackgroundImageSource` is a local name for this exact structural contract, not an exported type:

```ts
interface CropperBackgroundImageSource {
	getState: () => CropperState | null;
	getTransitions: () => CropperTransitions;
	getImage: () => CropperImage | null;
}
```

A matching cropper or preview snippet argument can be spread directly into this primitive.

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="cropper-source">CropperSource</h2>

Hidden source image for custom drawing. bind:element exposes HTMLImageElement or null; changing src replaces the image element. Also accepts HTMLImgAttributes except src and lowercase crossorigin, which are replaced by the props listed here.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `src` | `string` \| `null` | `undefined` |
| `crossOrigin` | `'anonymous'` \| `'use-credentials'` \| `boolean` | `true` |
| `element` | `HTMLImageElement` \| `null` | `null` |

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="cropper-preview-wrapper">CropperPreviewWrapper</h2>

Fades children according to preview.isLoaded(). The optional preview requires only isLoaded and may be null.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `preview` | `CropperPreviewWrapperSource` \| `null` | `undefined` |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `children` | `Snippet` | `undefined` |

`CropperPreviewWrapperSource` is a local name for this exact structural contract, not an exported type:

```ts
interface CropperPreviewWrapperSource {
	isLoaded: () => boolean;
}
```

A matching cropper or preview snippet argument can be spread directly into this primitive.

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

<h2 id="cropper-preview-background">CropperPreviewBackground</h2>

Positions the image with getPreviewStyle and the fitted size. The required preview supplies getState, getImage and getTransitions; transitions may be null. No export registration is needed.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `preview` | `CropperPreviewBackgroundSource` | Required |
| `crossOrigin` | `'anonymous'` \| `'use-credentials'` \| `boolean` | `true` |
| `size` | `Size` \| `null` | `undefined` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |

`CropperPreviewBackgroundSource` is a local name for this exact structural contract, not an exported type:

```ts
interface CropperPreviewBackgroundSource {
	getState: () => CropperState | null;
	getTransitions: () => CropperTransitions | null;
	getImage: () => CropperImage | null;
}
```

A matching cropper or preview snippet argument can be spread directly into this primitive.

Selectors are listed in the [complete styling inventory](/docs/reference/styling).

## Canvas export

The output and scratch canvases are internal. Use `CropperInstance.getCanvas()` to draw a crop; use the background snippet's `attachSource` to supply custom pixels. The internal canvas and transition elements have stable selectors but are not public component exports.
